.TH GIT-FEEDBACK 1 2026-10-14 "git-feedback 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-feedback, fdbk \- review any git diff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git feedback
.RB [ \-C
.IR dir ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B fdbk
.RB [ \-C
.IR dir ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fdbk
keeps code reviews of any diff that
.BR git\-diff (1)
can show: a branch, a commit, the index or the worktree.
Comments live in threads anchored to lines of the diff.
Each refresh records the current code as a numbered revision and moves
threads to their new lines; threads whose lines changed are marked outdated.
.PP
.B git feedback
and
.B fdbk
are the same program.
.SH REVIEW COMMANDS
.TP
\fBstart\fR [\fB\-\-title\fR \fIT\fR] [\fB\-\-new\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR] [\fIgit diff args\fR...]
Start a review of the diff, or resume the open review of the same diff.
.B \-\-new
always starts a new one.
Git diff options such as
.B \-\-cached
go after
.BR \-\- .
With no arguments, reviews what plain
.B git diff
shows: unstaged changes.
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-all ]
List open reviews, or all reviews with
.BR \-\-all .
.TP
.BR show " [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-no\-refresh ]
Refresh the review, then print unresolved threads with code context.
.B \-\-all
includes resolved threads.
.TP
.B refresh
Resolve the diff again, record a new revision if the code changed,
and move threads.
.TP
.BR close " | " reopen " | " rm
Close, reopen or delete the review.
.SH COMMENT COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcomment\fR [\fB\-\-path\fR \fIP\fR [\fB\-\-line\fR \fIN\fR [\fB\-\-start\-line\fR \fIM\fR]] [\fB\-\-side old\fR|\fBnew\fR]] [\fB\-\-revision\fR \fIN\fR] \fIBODY\fR
Start a thread on a line or line range, on a whole file (only
.BR \-\-path ),
or on the whole review (no
.BR \-\-path ).
.B \-\-side old
comments on the base side of the diff.
.TP
.BI reply " thread BODY"
Reply to a thread.
.TP
.BI edit " comment BODY"
Replace the text of a comment.
.TP
.BI delete " comment"
Delete a comment.
.TP
\fBresolve\fR \fIthread\fR | \fBunresolve\fR \fIthread\fR
Mark a thread resolved or unresolved.
.PP
.I BODY
is
.BI \-\-body " text"
or
.BI \-\-body\-file " file"
.RB ( \- " for stdin)."
Comment authors default to git's
.BR user.name ;
.BI \-\-author " name"
and
.B \-\-agent
override them.
Inside an agent harness, authors default to the agent; see
.BR ENVIRONMENT .
.SH GITHUB COMMANDS
These call the
.BR gh (1)
CLI, which must be logged in to the host.
.I pr
is a pull request number,
.IR owner / repo # n ,
or a pull request URL.
.TP
.BI "github start" " pr"
Fetch the pull request, start a review of
.IR base ... head ,
and import its comments.
.TP
.BI "github link" " pr"
Link the current review to a pull request.
.TP
.B github pull
Import new comments, edits and resolution changes.
.TP
\fBgithub push\fR [\fB\-\-event approve\fR|\fBrequest\-changes\fR|\fBcomment\fR] [\fB\-\-body\fR \fItext\fR]
Submit new comments as a review, and send replies, edits and resolution changes.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " dir"
Run as if started in
.IR dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-review " id"
Choose a review by id or unique id prefix.
By default,
.B $FDBK_REVIEW
is used, or the only open review.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON instead of text.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.B git feedback \-\-help
shows this page instead.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FDBK_REVIEW
Review to use when
.B \-\-review
is not given.
.TP
.B FDBK_AUTHOR
Default comment author name.
.TP
.B FDBK_AUTHOR_KIND
Set to
.B agent
to mark comments as written by an agent, or to
.B human
to turn off agent detection.
.TP
.BR AI_AGENT ", " CLAUDECODE ", " CODEX_THREAD_ID ", " OPENCODE ", ..."
Set by agent harnesses in the shells they run.
When one is present and
.B FDBK_AUTHOR_KIND
is unset, comments are marked as written by an agent and the author
defaults to the agent's name:
the value of
.BR AI_AGENT ,
or
.BR claude ,
.BR codex
or
.BR opencode .
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB "$(git rev-parse \-\-git\-common\-dir)" /git\-feedback/reviews/ id .json
Review files, shared by all worktrees of a repository.
.TP
.BI refs/git\-feedback/ id /
Refs that keep each revision's code from being garbage collected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-diff (1),
.BR gh (1)
